<!-- M19 post-milestone design review (issue #206): design-language.md's status table specifies an
     icon per status ("color + icon + word, never color alone" — RoomCardViewModel's own comment
     said as much and nothing consumed it). One geometry set, drawn by hand at a 16x16 grid so
     every status icon shares stroke weight and proportion — status is told by shape, color is
     reinforcement, not the only signal. Stroke-based (Path, not PathIcon) so line glyphs
     (check/cross/ring) don't need a closed fill area. -->
<ResourceDictionary xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">

  <!-- Succeeded: checkmark -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Icon.Check">M 3,8.5 L 6.5,12 L 13,4</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- Failed: cross -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Icon.Cross">M 4,4 L 12,12 M 12,4 L 4,12</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- Idle (hollow) / NeedsYou (filled) — one circle, two fill treatments at the call site. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Icon.Dot">M 13,8 A 5,5 0 1 1 3,8 A 5,5 0 1 1 13,8 Z</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- Running: an open ring — the static frame of a spinner (no motion in this pass, #208 owns animation). -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Icon.Ring">M 8,3 A 5,5 0 1 1 3.66,10.5</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- A circular arrow — the Retry action (and formerly the stale-list status, now Icon.Slashed).
       #461 redrew this: the original was "M 12.8,5.2 A 5,5 0 1 0 13,8 …", whose start point is 5.56
       from the centre, not 5. SVG silently scales radii up until both endpoints fit, so the arc was
       never the circle it was drawn as; and its "arrowhead" was two segments meeting at ~90° with
       one of them collinear with the tangent, which renders as a corner rather than an arrow. It
       read as broken because it was. Both endpoints are now exactly on r=5 about (8,8) — a 290°
       sweep leaving the gap at the top — with a proper chevron head along the tangent. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Icon.Refresh">M 10.87,3.9 A 5,5 0 1 1 5.13,3.9 M 10.05,1.64 L 10.87,3.9 L 8.47,3.9</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- #458: the two marks #334's five states needed and this set did not have. Named for their
       shape, because design/tokens.json addresses them by shape name and the drift gate resolves
       "Icon." + the name — a status whose mark has no geometry here fails CI rather than rendering
       as a blank space.

       The five status marks are Ring (working), Diamond (needs input), Page (ready for review),
       Check (finished) and Cross (failed). They are chosen to differ in *silhouette*: round-open,
       angular-solid, tall-rectangular, angular-line, angular-X. That is what decision 0006's rule
       actually asks for — five marks distinguishable only once you can see their colour would
       satisfy a literal reading of "carries a glyph" and fail the people the rule is for. -->

  <!-- Needs input: a filled speech bubble. #334's own description of this state is "an ordinary
       chat turn ... it is not awaiting approval, it is awaiting input", so the mark says *reply*.
       Filled rather than stroked because this is the loudest state in the set — it is the one
       actually asking something of you. (#461 replaced a solid diamond here, which reviewed as a
       gem rather than an alert.) -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Icon.Bubble">M 3,3.5 L 13,3.5 L 13,10.5 L 7,10.5 L 4.5,13.5 L 4.5,10.5 L 3,10.5 Z</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- Ready for review: an eye — there is a result here for your eyes to judge. (#461 replaced a
       page-with-turned-corner, which reviewed as "a document" rather than "review this".) -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Icon.Eye">M 2.5,8 C 5,3.6 11,3.6 13.5,8 C 11,12.4 5,12.4 2.5,8 Z M 9.9,8 A 1.9,1.9 0 1 1 6.1,8 A 1.9,1.9 0 1 1 9.9,8 Z</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- Cancelled: a dash. Deliberately NOT the filled square that suggests itself — a square is
       universally a *stop control*, this app needs a real stop affordance for a running session,
       and a state that looks like an action is a trap (owner review, #461). A bare bar reads
       "no outcome", which is exactly what a cancelled run has, and stays quiet: stopping something
       on purpose is not a failure and must not be dressed as one. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Icon.Dash">M 3.5,8 L 12.5,8</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- Stopped (#1219): a square — the run halted without finishing and without anyone stopping it,
       because its process died. The one hard-edged silhouette in the set, which is the point: every
       other status mark is built from circles, arcs and strokes, so this one is separable at row size
       and in a photocopy, per the token block's silhouette rule. Deliberately the universal stop
       shape rather than something alarming — a stopped room is not a failed one, and it resumes. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Icon.Square">M 3.5,3.5 L 12.5,3.5 L 12.5,12.5 L 3.5,12.5 Z</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- Queued: an ellipsis — waiting its turn, nothing has happened yet. Filled dots so it holds at
       row size, where stroked circles this small collapse into mush. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Icon.Ellipsis">M 5.55,8 A 1.35,1.35 0 1 1 2.85,8 A 1.35,1.35 0 1 1 5.55,8 Z M 9.35,8 A 1.35,1.35 0 1 1 6.65,8 A 1.35,1.35 0 1 1 9.35,8 Z M 13.15,8 A 1.35,1.35 0 1 1 10.45,8 A 1.35,1.35 0 1 1 13.15,8 Z</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- Unavailable: a slashed circle — recorded in the list but no longer readable. The international
       "not available" mark, and unmistakable against Icon.Cross (two diagonals, no circle) and
       Icon.Ring (an open arc, no slash). -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Icon.Slashed">M 13,8 A 5,5 0 1 1 3,8 A 5,5 0 1 1 13,8 Z M 4.5,11.5 L 11.5,4.5</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- #218: navigation rail + common actions, same 16x16 hand-drawn stroke set as the status
       icons above — Approve reuses Icon.Check and Reject reuses Icon.Cross (the issue's own
       "approve/check", "reject/cross" pairing); Retry reuses Icon.Refresh (an "again" arrow
       already exists, no need for a near-duplicate). Only the four genuinely new glyphs live
       here: Home, Task, Author, and Folder (the picker button, #212). -->

  <!-- A checklist — three list lines, the last one shorter (owner feedback: both the original
       two-circles-and-a-diagonal draft *and* the flowchart-node draft that replaced it still read
       as an old telephone handset at 14x14 — a branching-node glyph reads as a graph only at a
       size big enough to show its joints, which this rail icon isn't. A list needs no such
       resolution, and "task" maps to "item on a list" as directly as "author" maps to a pencil. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Icon.Task">M 3,4 L 13,4 M 3,8 L 13,8 M 3,12 L 9,12</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- A pencil — authoring. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Icon.Author">M 3,13 L 3.8,10.2 L 10.3,3.7 L 12.3,5.7 L 5.8,12.2 Z M 9.1,4.9 L 11.1,6.9</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- A folder — the browse/open action. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Icon.Folder">M 2,5.5 L 6,5.5 L 7.3,7 L 14,7 L 14,12.5 L 2,12.5 Z</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- A gear — the Settings nav destination (#1068), the universal settings glyph. Eight teeth
       radiating from a stroked body ring, with a centre hole; the corpus (02-screens) treats the
       rail glyphs as stand-ins, so this is the conventional icon, drawn to the same 16x16 stroke grid. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Icon.Settings">M 12.5,8 L 14,8 M 11.18,11.18 L 12.24,12.24 M 8,12.5 L 8,14 M 4.82,11.18 L 3.76,12.24 M 3.5,8 L 2,8 M 4.82,4.82 L 3.76,3.76 M 8,3.5 L 8,2 M 11.18,4.82 L 12.24,3.76 M 12.5,8 A 4.5,4.5 0 1 1 3.5,8 A 4.5,4.5 0 1 1 12.5,8 M 9.9,8 A 1.9,1.9 0 1 1 6.1,8 A 1.9,1.9 0 1 1 9.9,8</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- A speech bubble with a tail — Chat nav destination (M24 Phase 1, #262). -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Icon.Chat">M 3,4 L 13,4 L 13,10 L 6.5,10 L 4,13 L 4,10 L 3,10 Z</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- A 2x2 grid of squares — Tasks nav destination (M24 Phase 5, #278): the fleet management view,
       distinct from Icon.Task's single checklist (three list lines) since this represents many
       task/session directories at once, not one task's steps. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Icon.Fleet">M 2.5,2.5 L 6.8,2.5 L 6.8,6.8 L 2.5,6.8 Z M 9.2,2.5 L 13.5,2.5 L 13.5,6.8 L 9.2,6.8 Z M 2.5,9.2 L 6.8,9.2 L 6.8,13.5 L 2.5,13.5 Z M 9.2,9.2 L 13.5,9.2 L 13.5,13.5 L 9.2,13.5 Z</StreamGeometry>

  <!-- M22 template-picker vendor icons (issue #250 review follow-up): closed, fillable shapes (same
       16x16 grid as the set above), each a distinct point-count silhouette so the two read apart
       even without color. Claude: a 6-point sunburst. Gemini: a 4-point sparkle/diamond — fewer,
       fatter points than Claude's, deliberately, so shape alone (not just brand color) tells them
       apart. Neither reproduces the real vendor mark; both are original abstractions. -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Icon.Vendor.Claude">M 8,2 L 9.2,5.9 L 13.2,5 L 10.4,8 L 13.2,11 L 9.2,10.1 L 8,14 L 6.8,10.1 L 2.8,11 L 5.6,8 L 2.8,5 L 6.8,5.9 Z</StreamGeometry>
  <!-- vocabulary-ok: technical resource key -->
  <StreamGeometry x:Key="Icon.Vendor.Gemini">M 8,1.5 L 9.4,6.6 L 14.5,8 L 9.4,9.4 L 8,14.5 L 6.6,9.4 L 1.5,8 L 6.6,6.6 Z</StreamGeometry>

</ResourceDictionary>
